{
  "dom_id": "step-e3667",
  "name": "Example: Using Alternative Forms of Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Expressions",
  "problem": "Express $2\\cos^2{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\\right)}-1$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n2 \\cos^2 x - 1 = \\cos 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{cos}^{2}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-1 & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
